## Data and prior work
State/composition manifests and actual summaries were inspected and marked reused, not independently replicated. GEO metadata were freshly resolved for GSE137947/GSE138577/GSE177037/GSE241269. The P5 metadata explicitly pair gates by subject 1–4; the SNAT paper says each P5 sample is from one mouse. GSE138577 contains 3 P1 pools and 3 P60 pools, not 6 neonatal donors. P1 cells were deliberately depleted of eYFP-positive Schwann cells to approximately 30%. The 16-library rat repair design has only 2 libraries per compartment/time; purified-cell inputs contain at least 10 nerves. No donor pairing across compartments is established by labels 1/2.

After examining reference summary outcomes, a small retrospective gene-level/leave-one-subject audit of the existing P5 matrix is justified to distinguish cancellation within an antioxidant panel from a uniform gene response. This is not another atlas rerun or a new locked test. Use 4 subjects, log2(RPKM+0.1), paired t intervals and exact paired sign-flip enumeration, with pseudocount 0/1 sensitivities for measured positive targets and leave-one-subject means. Include all four genes separately, Pmp22 and seven myelin controls, not selected significant genes. No naive donor-level inference for pooled repair or dissociated cells. An optional native count sensitivity acquisition failed and will not be invented.

## Findings
The executed paired-gate audit reproduces the inherited four aggregate P5 effects within 2e-15 and adds an explicit gene-level/donor-sensitivity result: nmSC-minus-mSC Pmp22 -3.039, Nqo1 +1.085, Hmox1 -0.994, Gclc -0.021, Gclm -0.478 (log2(RPKM+0.1)). Pmp22/Nqo1/Hmox1 directions are consistent in all four subjects, every leave-one-subject mean, and pseudocounts 0/0.1/1. The near-null four-gene average (-0.102) contains opposing genes, not a uniform null. Paired-t intervals are descriptive; exact sign-flip p=0.125 for each of these consistent-direction endpoints prevents an assumption-light p<0.05 claim with four units. These are normal enriched-gate associations, neither pure-state causal changes nor Nae1 replication.

